{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stuckup-trophic-nabarlek","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nFault-seeding under afa0-2e15 (rival-ammoniacal-crustacean) proved a real detection gap in\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py`.\n\n`_assert_complete_or_loud` stops at `isinstance(doc, expected_shape)`. Two seeded faults —\nF3 (`show` emits `{}`, exit 0) and F6 (`show` emits a record with `ticket_id` removed,\nexit 0) — passed BOTH generic tests while the original regression\n`test_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst` went RED on each.\n\nSo the generic property currently certifies a read as \"COMPLETE-or-LOUD\" when the payload is\nshape-valid but content-hollow. The gap applies to all four surfaces (show/list/search/ready),\nnot just show — nothing in the property asserts that a returned record carries identity.\n\nNote: this is a gap against the property's INTENT, not against its docstring (which promises\nshape only). Closing it is a deliberate strengthening, not a bug fix.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a per-surface content-completeness predicate to the SURFACES table (e.g. show -> the\n  object carries a truthy `ticket_id`; list/ready/search -> every element that is present\n  carries one, with valid-empty `[]` still passing).\n- Prove RED first by re-applying seeds F3 and F6 from afa0-2e15 (`/tmp/faultseed/seeds.py`,\n  recorded in that ticket's matrix comment), then GREEN on the restored tree.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- With F3 seeded, both generic tests must go RED (they currently pass).\n- With F6 seeded, both generic tests must go RED (they currently pass).\n- Unseeded tree: `pytest tests/interfaces/store/` GREEN.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Seeded fault F3 is detected by the generic property.\n- [ ] Seeded fault F6 is detected by the generic property.\n- [ ] Valid-empty results (`[]`) still pass, remaining distinguishable from truncated output.\n- [ ] No increase in the property's wall-clock runtime.\n- [ ] The original regression test is left unchanged by this ticket.","id":"8469-85a7-88b7-4bbb","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-quality","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Generic reads-under-contention property accepts partial-success payloads on all four surfaces"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787172698189640001,"uuid":"73e16b6e-813c-471a-aa24-a497af521667"}